ion polls are available, so the assessment rests on fundamentals, expert ratings and campaign finance.\n\nNational raters split between Safe D and Likely D, and prediction markets price a Pou win at roughly 96 to 97 percent. Pou has raised about six times as much money as Pino and holds a wide cash-on-hand advantage, while outside spending has been minimal on both sides. A Republican group has funded advertising in two New Jersey House districts, a reminder that the seat sits on the competitive edge of the map. Pou remains the strong favorite, with the main risk being a late outside-spending push that narrows the margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9625, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9596, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9671, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9566, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9611, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9669, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9744, "margin": 13.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9657, "margin": 12.8}]}